[32m+[m[32m## Website SEO Requirements[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32mApply these requirements whenever creating or modifying a public HTML page, page template, route, image, sitemap, robots file, or structured-data file:[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m- Use one clear search intent per indexable page and write original, useful content for that intent.[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m- Use a unique, descriptive `<title>`, meta description, canonical URL, Open Graph title/description/URL/type/image, and X/Twitter card metadata on every indexable page.[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m- Use exactly one visible, descriptive `<h1>` per page and maintain a logical heading hierarchy with `<h2>` and `<h3>`.[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m- Use lowercase, descriptive, hyphenated URLs. Prefer stable directory paths such as `/services/plant-design/` over vague names, query-only pages, or filenames with unnecessary extensions.[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m- Add inline, valid JSON-LD that matches visible page content. Use the appropriate schema type such as `Organization`, `WebSite`, `WebPage`, `Service`, `BreadcrumbList`, or `Article`.[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m- Use `FAQPage` structured data only when the questions and answers are visibly present and genuinely useful. Never add unsupported reviews, awards, prices, partners, events, or claims to schema.[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m- Use canonical URLs in JSON-LD, internal links, Open Graph data, and sitemaps consistently. Do not include URL fragments, redirects, duplicate pages, private files, or non-indexable campaign pages in the XML sitemap.[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m- Give every meaningful image accurate, natural `alt` text describing what is visible and its purpose. Use `alt=""` for decorative images. Do not stuff keywords into alt text or use the filename as alt text.[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m- Use semantic HTML, accessible labels, keyboard-visible focus states, responsive layouts, sufficient color contrast, descriptive link text, and reduced-motion support.[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m- Do not hide important information in images. Repeat any important visual label, claim, or service name as nearby HTML text.[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m- Validate HTML, links, metadata, canonical URLs, JSON-LD, sitemap URLs, mobile rendering, performance, and accessibility before considering a page complete.[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m- Do not publish unsupported statistics, certifications, customer logos, partnerships, locations, reviews, or technical claims. Confirm business facts before adding them to page copy or structured data.[m[41m[m
